<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch05-vector-valued-functions" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Vector-Valued Functions and Motion</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>We now apply single-variable calculus to the parametrized curves of Chapter 4. Component derivatives and integrals lead to velocity, arc length, curvature, and the Frenet frame and torsion of space curves. Polar motion then provides a second example of a moving frame, before the chapter review gathers these tools in applications.</p>
  </introduction>

